WEBVTT

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:28.691
I can't believe we
actually bought this thing.

00:00:28.724 --> 00:00:31.324
There's a reason charity
auctions have an open bar.

00:00:31.357 --> 00:00:33.257
Don't you think...

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.390
I don't know, it's kind of creepy?

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:39.457
It's okay.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.958
I'll keep you safe.

00:00:43.058 --> 00:00:45.390
Maybe you're the one i
ought to be scared of.

00:00:47.457 --> 00:00:50.557
Mmm. Let's go upstairs.

00:00:50.591 --> 00:00:53.691
Give me 10 minutes to lock up.

00:00:53.724 --> 00:00:55.591
Mmm.

00:00:55.624 --> 00:00:57.123
Make than one minute.

00:01:46.657 --> 00:01:49.958
If you don't hurry up, i'm
gonna start without you!

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:12.891
Babe, get the lights.
I can't see a thing.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.857
Do you smell something?

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:23.991
Ann?

00:02:26.657 --> 00:02:28.190
Ann?!

00:02:46.757 --> 00:02:49.357

...3-4-2-0.

00:02:50.424 --> 00:02:52.490
All right. You're in there.

00:02:52.524 --> 00:02:53.624
Perfect.

00:02:53.657 --> 00:02:56.390
So, is that brandi with a "y" or an "i"?

00:03:13.891 --> 00:03:16.924
All right, listen. I got to go.

00:03:16.958 --> 00:03:19.058
Hold that thought. I'll
be right back, okay?

00:03:21.123 --> 00:03:23.757
All right, so, i think i got
something. Oh, yeah, me too.

00:03:23.791 --> 00:03:25.724
I think we need to take
a little shore leave

00:03:25.757 --> 00:03:27.791
For just a little bit.
What do you think, huh?

00:03:27.824 --> 00:03:29.457
I'm so in the door with this one here.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.891
So, what are we today,
dean? Are we rock stars?

00:03:31.924 --> 00:03:33.223
Are we army rangers?

00:03:33.257 --> 00:03:35.924
We're l.A. Tv scouts looking
for people with special skills.

00:03:37.024 --> 00:03:39.058
But, hey, it's not that far off, right?

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.791
By the way, she's got
a friend over there.

00:03:41.824 --> 00:03:43.657
I can probably hook you
up. What do you think?

00:03:43.691 --> 00:03:45.424
Dean, uh, no thanks.
I can get my own dates.

00:03:45.457 --> 00:03:47.524
Yeah, you can, but you don't.

00:03:47.557 --> 00:03:49.591
What is that supposed to mean?

00:03:49.624 --> 00:03:51.324
Nothing. What do you got?

00:03:51.357 --> 00:03:53.891
Mark and ann telesca
of new paltz, new york,

00:03:53.924 --> 00:03:56.991
Were both found dead in their
home just a few days ago.

00:03:57.024 --> 00:03:58.857
Throats were slit, there were no prints,

00:03:58.891 --> 00:04:00.657
No murder weapons, all
- Dean?

00:04:00.691 --> 00:04:01.958
No prints, no murder weapons,

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:03.958
All doors and windows were
locked from the inside.

00:04:03.991 --> 00:04:06.058
Could just be a garden-Variety murder.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.390
You know, not our department.
No, dad says different.

00:04:08.424 --> 00:04:09.457
What do you mean?

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:10.457
Look.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:11.657
Dad noted three murders

00:04:11.691 --> 00:04:13.591
In the same area of upstate new york.

00:04:13.624 --> 00:04:16.157
First one, right here, 1912.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:19.958
The second one in 1945,
and the third in 1970.

00:04:19.991 --> 00:04:22.524
The same m.O. As the telescas
- The throats were slit,

00:04:22.557 --> 00:04:24.324
The houses were locked from the inside.

00:04:24.357 --> 00:04:25.891
So much time passed between the murders

00:04:25.924 --> 00:04:27.724
That nobody checked the
pattern except for dad.

00:04:27.757 --> 00:04:29.757
He always kept his eyes
peeled for another one.

00:04:29.791 --> 00:04:31.123
And now we got one. Exactly.

00:04:31.157 --> 00:04:33.357
All right. I'm with you.
It's worth checking out.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:35.624
We can't pick this up till
first thing, though, right?

00:04:35.657 --> 00:04:37.958
Yeah. Good.

00:04:37.991 --> 00:04:39.457
Dean...

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:40.924
Ladies. Did you miss me?

00:04:40.958 --> 00:04:42.624
I'm just kidding.

00:04:42.657 --> 00:04:45.490
Listen, i talked to my
producer, and it is looking good.

00:05:01.958 --> 00:05:03.857
Oh, man, that's so not cool.

00:05:03.891 --> 00:05:07.357
I just swept the telesca
house with the emf. It's clean.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:10.024
And last night, while you were...

00:05:10.058 --> 00:05:11.290
Out...

00:05:11.324 --> 00:05:12.624
Oh, good times.

00:05:12.657 --> 00:05:14.290
...i checked the history of the house.

00:05:14.324 --> 00:05:15.924
No hauntings, no violent crimes,

00:05:15.958 --> 00:05:18.457
Nothing strange about the
telescas themselves, either.

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:20.791
So if it's not the people
and it's not the house,

00:05:20.824 --> 00:05:22.390
Then maybe it's the contents -

00:05:22.424 --> 00:05:24.591
A cursed object or
something. House is clean.

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:25.991
You said that.

00:05:26.024 --> 00:05:27.024
No, i mean it's empty.

00:05:27.058 --> 00:05:29.058
No furniture, nothing.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:31.390
Where's all their stuff?

00:05:59.424 --> 00:06:02.524
Silent auctions, estate sales -

00:06:02.557 --> 00:06:05.190
It's like a garage sale for
w.A.S.P.S, if you ask me.

00:06:05.223 --> 00:06:06.557
Can i help you, gentlemen?

00:06:09.223 --> 00:06:12.090
I'd like some champagne, please.

00:06:12.123 --> 00:06:13.857
He's not a waiter.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.424
I'm sam connors.

00:06:20.457 --> 00:06:23.058
This is my brother, dean.

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:25.223
We are art dealers with connors limited.

00:06:25.257 --> 00:06:27.190
You're art dealers? That's right.

00:06:27.223 --> 00:06:29.624
I'm daniel blake. This
is my auction house.

00:06:29.657 --> 00:06:32.824
Now, gentlemen, this
is a private showing,

00:06:32.857 --> 00:06:35.757
And i don't remember seeing
you on the guest list.

00:06:35.791 --> 00:06:37.090
We're there, chuckles.

00:06:37.123 --> 00:06:39.290
You just need to take another look.

00:06:39.324 --> 00:06:40.724
Oh, finally.

00:06:43.257 --> 00:06:44.524
Cheers.

00:07:02.591 --> 00:07:05.791
A fine example of american
primitive, wouldn't you say?

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:14.691
Well, i'd say it's more
grant wood than grandma moses

00:07:16.324 --> 00:07:17.757
But you knew that.

00:07:17.791 --> 00:07:19.424
You just wanted to see if i did.

00:07:19.457 --> 00:07:21.257
Guilty.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.958
And clumsy. I apologize.

00:07:23.991 --> 00:07:25.924
I'm sarah blake.

00:07:25.958 --> 00:07:28.524
I'm sam.

00:07:28.557 --> 00:07:32.991
This is my...brother, dean.

00:07:33.024 --> 00:07:34.424
Dean. Hmm.

00:07:34.457 --> 00:07:36.090
Can we get you some more mini quiche?

00:07:36.123 --> 00:07:38.657
Mnh-Mnh, i'm good. Thanks.

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:41.123
So, can i help you with something?

00:07:41.157 --> 00:07:43.490
Yeah, actually.

00:07:43.524 --> 00:07:46.357
What can you tell us
about the telesca estate?

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:48.557
The whole thing's pretty
grisly if you ask me,

00:07:48.591 --> 00:07:50.557
Selling their things this soon.

00:07:50.591 --> 00:07:52.691
But dad's right about one thing -

00:07:52.724 --> 00:07:54.958
Sensationalism brings out the crowds.

00:07:54.991 --> 00:07:57.424
Even the rich ones.

00:08:00.223 --> 00:08:02.290
Is it possible to see the provenances?

00:08:02.324 --> 00:08:06.123
I'm afraid there isn't
any chance of that.

00:08:06.157 --> 00:08:08.123
Why not?

00:08:08.157 --> 00:08:09.724
You're not on the guest list...

00:08:09.757 --> 00:08:11.290
And i think it's time to leave.

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:13.324
Well, we don't have to be
told twice. Apparently, you do.

00:08:13.357 --> 00:08:14.390
Okay, it's all right.

00:08:14.424 --> 00:08:17.290
We don't want any trouble. We'll go.

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:26.457
Dad, that was rude.

00:08:29.357 --> 00:08:31.791
Grant wood, grandma moses
- What?

00:08:31.824 --> 00:08:33.157
Art history course.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:34.757
It's good for meeting girls.

00:08:34.791 --> 00:08:36.591
It's like i don't even know you.

00:08:53.591 --> 00:08:54.691
Huh.Huh.

00:08:54.724 --> 00:08:56.891
And what was the providence?

00:08:56.924 --> 00:08:58.024
Provenance.

00:08:58.058 --> 00:08:59.490
It's a certificate of origin,

00:08:59.524 --> 00:09:00.857
Like a biography, you know?

00:09:00.891 --> 00:09:03.123
We can use them to track
the history of the pieces,

00:09:03.157 --> 00:09:04.857
See if anything's got a freaky past.

00:09:04.891 --> 00:09:07.223
We're not getting
anything out of chuckles,

00:09:07.257 --> 00:09:08.691
But, uh, sarah... yeah.

00:09:08.724 --> 00:09:10.591
Maybe you can get her
to write it on a napkin.

00:09:10.624 --> 00:09:12.024
Not me.

00:09:12.058 --> 00:09:13.424
Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:09:13.457 --> 00:09:15.123
Pickups are your thing, dean.

00:09:15.157 --> 00:09:17.290
It wasn't my butt she was checking out.

00:09:17.324 --> 00:09:20.624
In other words, you want me
to use her to get information.

00:09:20.657 --> 00:09:22.190
Sometimes you got to
take one for the team.

00:09:22.223 --> 00:09:24.724
Call sarah.

00:09:29.058 --> 00:09:30.490
Nice place.

00:09:30.524 --> 00:09:31.624
Yeah.

00:09:39.991 --> 00:09:41.090
Glad you called.

00:09:42.157 --> 00:09:44.324
Surprised, but glad.

00:09:44.357 --> 00:09:45.390
Yeah?

00:09:45.424 --> 00:09:47.223
Although you seemed to have a hard time

00:09:47.257 --> 00:09:49.624
Getting out the words, "would
you like to have dinner?"

00:09:49.657 --> 00:09:51.724
Yeah.

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:54.924
I haven't really been
on a date in a while.

00:09:54.958 --> 00:09:56.390
Welcome to the club.

00:09:56.424 --> 00:09:58.857
You're kidding me.

00:09:58.891 --> 00:10:02.657
Man: here we are.

00:10:02.691 --> 00:10:04.290
The wine list.

00:10:17.691 --> 00:10:22.424
I don't know about romeo
here, but i'll have a beer.

00:10:24.724 --> 00:10:25.757
And you?

00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:27.090
I will, too.

00:10:27.123 --> 00:10:28.157
Certainly.

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:30.524
Sam: so, you studied art in school, huh?

00:10:30.557 --> 00:10:31.591
Sarah: it's true.

00:10:31.624 --> 00:10:32.691
I was an artist -

00:10:32.724 --> 00:10:36.657
A terrible, terrible artist.

00:10:36.691 --> 00:10:38.657
That's why i'm in the auction business.

00:10:38.691 --> 00:10:40.190
And you were pre-Law?

00:10:40.223 --> 00:10:41.290
Yeah.

00:10:41.324 --> 00:10:44.290
But you didn't go to
law school. How come?

00:10:44.324 --> 00:10:48.024
Uh, it's a really long
story for another time.

00:10:48.058 --> 00:10:50.657
You're not like any art
dealer i've ever met.

00:10:55.757 --> 00:10:58.058
So...what did you mean when you said

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.724
You hadn't been on a date in a while?

00:10:59.757 --> 00:11:01.490
Trying to make me feel
like i'm not such a loser?

00:11:01.524 --> 00:11:03.223
I'm sure many things, sam.

00:11:03.257 --> 00:11:06.390
I'm also sure "loser" isn't one of them.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:13.490
It was my mom.

00:11:13.524 --> 00:11:15.757
She died about a year ago.

00:11:15.791 --> 00:11:18.357
Totally unexpected.

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:21.824
It really threw me.

00:11:23.524 --> 00:11:29.190
I went into this shell
- A nice, warm, safe shell.

00:11:29.223 --> 00:11:31.991
But lately, i've been thinking...

00:11:32.024 --> 00:11:35.624
It's not what she would
have wanted for me.

00:11:35.657 --> 00:11:37.123
So...

00:11:42.257 --> 00:11:43.557
So, what about you?

00:11:43.591 --> 00:11:46.290
You're a reasonably attractive guy.

00:11:47.958 --> 00:11:49.691
Reasonably.

00:11:49.724 --> 00:11:52.891
Why haven't you been out and about?

00:12:01.123 --> 00:12:04.824
Another long story for another time.

00:12:10.991 --> 00:12:12.857
So, she just handed the
providences over to you?

00:12:12.891 --> 00:12:14.058
Provenances.

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:16.924
Provenances? Yes, we
went back to her place.

00:12:16.958 --> 00:12:19.257
I got a copy of the papers.

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:20.757
And?

00:12:20.791 --> 00:12:24.024
And nothing. That's it. I left.

00:12:24.058 --> 00:12:28.424
You didn't have to con her
or do any special favors?

00:12:28.457 --> 00:12:30.457
Would you get your mind
out of the gutter, please?

00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:32.991
When this whole thing's done,
we could stick around a bit.

00:12:33.024 --> 00:12:34.757
Why? So you could take her out again.

00:12:34.791 --> 00:12:36.624
It's obvious you're into
her. Even i can see that.

00:12:36.657 --> 00:12:38.924
Hey, all right. I think
i got something here.

00:12:43.157 --> 00:12:44.958
"Portrait of isaiah merchant's family,

00:12:44.991 --> 00:12:46.324
Painted 1910."

00:12:46.357 --> 00:12:48.424
Now compare the names of the
owners with dad's journal.

00:12:52.724 --> 00:12:56.490
"First purchased in 1912 to peter sims."

00:12:56.524 --> 00:12:58.724
Peter sims murdered, 1912.

00:13:02.791 --> 00:13:05.424
Same thing in 1945.

00:13:05.457 --> 00:13:07.958
Oh, same thing in 1970.

00:13:07.991 --> 00:13:09.223
Then stored,

00:13:09.257 --> 00:13:11.591
Until it was donated to a
charity auction last month,

00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:13.490
Where the telescas bought it.

00:13:13.524 --> 00:13:16.190
So, what do you think?
It's haunted or cursed?

00:13:16.223 --> 00:13:18.390
Either way, it's toast.

00:13:40.757 --> 00:13:42.324
Go ahead.

00:14:27.058 --> 00:14:28.424
Ugly-Ass thing.

00:14:28.457 --> 00:14:31.324
If you ask me, we're doing
the art world a favor.

00:15:00.974 --> 00:15:03.240
We got a problem. I
can't find my wallet.

00:15:03.974 --> 00:15:05.741
How's that my problem?

00:15:05.774 --> 00:15:09.108
'Cause i think i dropped it
in the warehouse last night.

00:15:09.141 --> 00:15:10.141
You're kidding, right?

00:15:10.174 --> 00:15:11.874
I mean, it's got my prints, my i.D. -

00:15:11.907 --> 00:15:13.974
Well, my fake i.D.,
anyway, but we got to get it

00:15:14.007 --> 00:15:15.807
Before somebody else finds it. Come on.

00:15:26.074 --> 00:15:28.141
How do you lose your wallet, dean?

00:15:29.907 --> 00:15:31.741
Hey, guys.

00:15:31.774 --> 00:15:34.041
Sarah. Hey.

00:15:34.074 --> 00:15:35.640
What are you doing here?

00:15:35.674 --> 00:15:37.874
Oh...

00:15:37.907 --> 00:15:39.240
We're
- We're leaving town,

00:15:39.273 --> 00:15:41.373
And, you know, we came to say goodbye.

00:15:41.407 --> 00:15:43.208
What are you talking about, sam?

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:46.041
We're sticking around for
at least another day or two.

00:15:46.074 --> 00:15:47.607
Oh, sam, by the way,

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:51.041
I wanted to give you
that 20 bucks i owe you.

00:15:51.074 --> 00:15:54.373
I always forget.

00:15:54.407 --> 00:15:56.474
There you go.

00:15:59.174 --> 00:16:00.974
Well, i'll leave you
two crazy kids alone.

00:16:01.007 --> 00:16:03.607
I got to go do... something...somewhere.

00:16:10.841 --> 00:16:12.741
So...

00:16:12.774 --> 00:16:14.141
I had a good time last night.

00:16:14.174 --> 00:16:16.174
Yeah. Yeah, i did, too.

00:16:16.208 --> 00:16:19.174
Maybe we should do it again sometime?

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:23.741
You know, i'd love to, i really would,

00:16:23.774 --> 00:16:25.574
But dean
- He was just screwing around.

00:16:25.607 --> 00:16:27.841
We really are taking off today.

00:16:27.874 --> 00:16:30.041
Oh. Oh.

00:16:30.074 --> 00:16:31.474
Now that's too bad.

00:16:31.507 --> 00:16:34.307
Oh, my god! What?

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:35.741
The -

00:16:35.774 --> 00:16:37.373
That painting...

00:16:37.407 --> 00:16:39.607
Looks so good.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:42.941
If you can call that monstrosity good,

00:16:42.974 --> 00:16:44.707
Then, yeah, i guess.

00:16:44.741 --> 00:16:46.741
Sarah, what do you know
about that painting?

00:16:46.774 --> 00:16:48.974
Not much. Just that it creeps me out.

00:16:49.007 --> 00:16:50.440
We sold it to the telescas

00:16:50.474 --> 00:16:52.440
At a charity auction the
night they were murdered.

00:16:52.474 --> 00:16:54.974
And now you're just gonna sell it again?

00:16:55.007 --> 00:16:57.907
As much as my dad wants
to, no. I won't let him.

00:16:57.941 --> 00:16:59.874
I think it'd be in bad taste.

00:16:59.907 --> 00:17:01.674
Good, yeah. You know what? Don't. Don't.

00:17:01.707 --> 00:17:03.307
Make sure you don't, okay? Why?

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:05.407
Don't tell me you're interested in that.

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:07.273
No, god, no. Not in buying it, no.

00:17:07.307 --> 00:17:09.874
I got to go. I got to
take care of something.

00:17:09.907 --> 00:17:11.440
But, um, i will call you back.

00:17:11.474 --> 00:17:13.007
I will call you. I'll see you later.

00:17:13.041 --> 00:17:15.373
Wait, so you're not leaving tonight?

00:17:15.407 --> 00:17:18.874
No, i guess not. I'll see you.

00:17:20.874 --> 00:17:22.741
Okay.

00:17:24.841 --> 00:17:27.841
I don't understand, dean.
We burned the damn thing.

00:17:27.874 --> 00:17:29.941
Yeah, thank you, captain obvious.

00:17:29.974 --> 00:17:33.907
We just need to figure out
another way to get rid of it.

00:17:33.941 --> 00:17:35.041
Any ideas?

00:17:35.074 --> 00:17:36.307
Okay, all right.

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:38.807
Well, um, in almost all the
lore about haunted paintings,

00:17:38.841 --> 00:17:40.574
It's always the painting's
subject that haunts them.

00:17:40.607 --> 00:17:42.373
Yeah? All right.

00:17:42.407 --> 00:17:44.874
So we need to figure out
everything there is to know

00:17:44.907 --> 00:17:47.640
About that creepy-Ass family
in that creepy-Ass painting.

00:17:47.674 --> 00:17:49.774
What were their names again?

00:17:50.807 --> 00:17:52.108
The isaiah merchant family, right?

00:17:52.141 --> 00:17:53.907
Yeah, that's right.

00:17:53.941 --> 00:17:57.407
I dug up every scrap of
local history i could find.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:59.440
So, uh, are you boys crime buffs?

00:17:59.474 --> 00:18:02.407
Kind of. Why do you ask?

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:03.774
Well...

00:18:07.373 --> 00:18:09.307
Yes. Yeah, that sounds about right.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:10.907
The whole family was killed?

00:18:10.941 --> 00:18:13.674
It seems this isaiah, he
slits his kids' throats,

00:18:13.707 --> 00:18:15.707
Then his wife, then himself.

00:18:15.741 --> 00:18:19.507
Now, he was a barber by
trade. Used a straight razor.

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:21.307
Why'd he do it?

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:23.607
Well, let's look.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:25.640
Uh, "people who knew
him described isaiah

00:18:25.674 --> 00:18:27.607
"As having a stern
and harsh temperament,

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:29.307
And controlled his
family with an iron fist."

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:34.108
Wife, two sons, adopted daughter
- Yeah, yeah.

00:18:34.141 --> 00:18:36.574
There were whispers that the
wife was gonna take the kids

00:18:36.607 --> 00:18:40.474
And leave, which, of course,
you know, in that day and age...

00:18:40.507 --> 00:18:43.607
So instead, old man isaiah,
well, he gave them all a shave.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.607
Kkkch!

00:18:46.874 --> 00:18:48.807
Does it say what happened to the bodies?

00:18:48.841 --> 00:18:50.307
They were all cremated.

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:55.041
Anything else? Yeah.

00:18:55.074 --> 00:18:57.974
Actually, i found a
picture of the family.

00:18:58.007 --> 00:18:59.774
It's right here somewhere.

00:18:59.807 --> 00:19:01.707
Right. Here it is.

00:19:09.807 --> 00:19:12.440
Hey, could we get a
copy of this, please?

00:19:12.474 --> 00:19:14.307
Sure.

00:19:18.407 --> 00:19:19.607
Dad...

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:22.807
You promised you wouldn't
sell that painting.

00:19:22.841 --> 00:19:24.674
I know, sweetie, but evelyn's offered

00:19:24.707 --> 00:19:26.208
A persuasive amount of money.

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:29.774
You're shameless, you know that?

00:19:29.807 --> 00:19:32.574
For that kind of money,
i can afford to be.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:39.240
Sam: i'm telling you,
man. I'm sure of it.

00:19:39.273 --> 00:19:41.774
The painting at the auction
house, dad is looking down.

00:19:41.807 --> 00:19:43.607
The painting here, dad's looking out.

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:44.974
The painting has changed, dean.

00:19:45.007 --> 00:19:47.307
So you think that daddy dearest
is trapped in the painting,

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:48.974
And he's handing out columbian neckties

00:19:49.007 --> 00:19:51.540
Like he did with his family?
Well, yeah, it seems like it.

00:19:51.574 --> 00:19:53.574
But if his bones are already dusted,

00:19:53.607 --> 00:19:55.407
Then how are we gonna stop him?

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:56.774
Well, if isaiah's position changed,

00:19:56.807 --> 00:19:58.874
Then maybe some other things in
the painting changed, as well.

00:19:58.907 --> 00:20:00.273
It could give us some clues.

00:20:00.307 --> 00:20:01.574
Like a "da vinci code" deal?

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:03.674
I don't know.

00:20:03.707 --> 00:20:06.273
I'm still waiting for
the movie on that one.

00:20:06.307 --> 00:20:08.373
Anyway, we got to get back
in and see that painting,

00:20:08.407 --> 00:20:10.440
Which is a good thing,
because you can get more time

00:20:10.474 --> 00:20:11.707
To crush on your girlfriend.

00:20:11.741 --> 00:20:13.974
Dude...enough already.

00:20:14.007 --> 00:20:16.007
What? "What?" Ever since we got here,

00:20:16.041 --> 00:20:18.108
You've been trying to
pimp me out to sarah.

00:20:18.141 --> 00:20:19.340
Just back off, all right?

00:20:19.373 --> 00:20:20.741
Well, you like her, don't you?

00:20:20.774 --> 00:20:22.440
All right, you like her. She likes you.

00:20:22.474 --> 00:20:24.007
You're both consenting adults.

00:20:24.041 --> 00:20:25.108
What's the point, dean?

00:20:25.141 --> 00:20:26.607
We'll just leave. We always leave.

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:28.373
Well, i'm not talking
about marriage, sam.

00:20:28.407 --> 00:20:30.307
I don't get it. What do
you care if i hook up?

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:32.208
Maybe you wouldn't be
so cranky all the time.

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:40.340
Seriously, sam, this isn't
about just hooking up, okay?

00:20:40.373 --> 00:20:43.340
I think that this sarah
girl could be good for you.

00:20:45.741 --> 00:20:49.108
And i don't mean any
disrespect, but i'm -

00:20:49.141 --> 00:20:51.074
I'm sure that this is
about jessica, right?

00:20:52.074 --> 00:20:56.874
Now, i don't know what it's like
to lose somebody like that...

00:20:56.907 --> 00:20:58.774
But...

00:20:58.807 --> 00:21:00.807
I would think that she
would want you to be happy.

00:21:03.108 --> 00:21:06.141
God forbid, have fun once in a while.

00:21:06.174 --> 00:21:07.373
Wouldn't she?

00:21:12.041 --> 00:21:13.807
Yeah, i know she would.

00:21:18.807 --> 00:21:24.240
Yeah, you're right. Part
of this is about jessica.

00:21:24.273 --> 00:21:25.640
But not the main part.

00:21:25.674 --> 00:21:27.574
What's it about?

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:33.707
Yeah, all right.

00:21:33.741 --> 00:21:36.707
Well, we still got to see that painting,

00:21:36.741 --> 00:21:40.108
Which means you still
got to call sarah, so...

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:54.074
Sarah, hey. It's sam.

00:21:54.108 --> 00:21:55.941
Hey, hi.

00:21:55.974 --> 00:21:58.208
Good, good, yeah. What about you?

00:21:58.240 --> 00:22:00.974
Yeah, good. Good, really good. Smooth.

00:22:01.007 --> 00:22:03.507
So, uh
- So, listen.

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:05.340
Me and my brother were thinking

00:22:05.373 --> 00:22:07.440
That maybe we'd like to come back in

00:22:07.474 --> 00:22:09.273
And look at the painting again.

00:22:09.307 --> 00:22:11.974
I think maybe we are
interested in buying it.

00:22:12.007 --> 00:22:13.174
Wait, what?

00:22:13.208 --> 00:22:16.307
Who'd you sell it to?

00:22:16.340 --> 00:22:18.841
Sarah, i need an address right now.

00:23:03.974 --> 00:23:05.108
Sam, what's happening?

00:23:05.140 --> 00:23:07.240
I told you you shouldn't have come.

00:23:10.774 --> 00:23:12.008
Hello, anybody home?!

00:23:12.041 --> 00:23:14.574
You said evelyn might be in
danger. What kind of danger?

00:23:14.607 --> 00:23:18.474
I can't knock this sucker
down. I got to pick it.

00:23:18.507 --> 00:23:21.041
What are you guys, burglars?

00:23:21.074 --> 00:23:22.374
I wish it was that simple.

00:23:22.407 --> 00:23:24.841
Look, you really should wait in the car.

00:23:24.874 --> 00:23:26.240
Ugh.

00:23:26.273 --> 00:23:27.741
The hell i will. Evelyn's a friend.

00:23:27.774 --> 00:23:28.807
Evelyn?

00:23:28.841 --> 00:23:30.407
Sam: evelyn!

00:23:35.307 --> 00:23:36.540
Evelyn?

00:23:47.074 --> 00:23:49.741
Evelyn?

00:23:49.774 --> 00:23:51.140
It's sarah blake.

00:23:51.173 --> 00:23:52.607
Are you all right?

00:23:52.641 --> 00:23:53.907
Sarah, don't! Sarah!

00:24:00.008 --> 00:24:02.707
Oh, my god! Oh, my god!

00:24:12.108 --> 00:24:14.874
Hey. You all right?

00:24:14.907 --> 00:24:16.307
No, actually.

00:24:16.340 --> 00:24:19.641
I just lied to the cops and told
them i went to evelyn's alone

00:24:19.674 --> 00:24:22.108
And found her like that.

00:24:22.140 --> 00:24:23.273
Thank you. Don't thank me.

00:24:23.307 --> 00:24:24.674
I'm about to call them right back

00:24:24.707 --> 00:24:26.540
If you don't tell me
what the hell is going on.

00:24:26.574 --> 00:24:28.041
Who's killing these people?

00:24:32.173 --> 00:24:33.741
"What."

00:24:33.774 --> 00:24:35.207
What?

00:24:35.240 --> 00:24:36.474
It's not "who."

00:24:36.507 --> 00:24:39.407
It's "what" is killing those people.

00:24:42.340 --> 00:24:44.907
Sarah, you saw that painting move.

00:24:44.941 --> 00:24:47.741
No.

00:24:47.774 --> 00:24:50.440
No, i was
- I was seeing things.

00:24:50.474 --> 00:24:51.807
It's impossible.

00:24:51.841 --> 00:24:53.507
Yeah, well, welcome to our world.

00:24:53.540 --> 00:24:56.774
Sarah, i know this sounds crazy...

00:24:56.807 --> 00:24:59.041
But we think that that
painting is haunted.

00:25:03.440 --> 00:25:04.941
You're joking.

00:25:09.240 --> 00:25:11.741
You're not joking.

00:25:11.774 --> 00:25:14.207
God, the guys i go out with.

00:25:14.240 --> 00:25:15.874
Sarah, think about it.

00:25:15.907 --> 00:25:19.574
Evelyn, the telescas
- They both had the painting.

00:25:19.607 --> 00:25:21.207
And there have been others before that.

00:25:21.240 --> 00:25:22.774
Wherever this thing goes, people die,

00:25:22.807 --> 00:25:25.173
And we're just trying to stop it...

00:25:25.207 --> 00:25:26.607
And that's the truth.

00:25:26.641 --> 00:25:31.507
Well, then, i guess you better show me.

00:25:31.540 --> 00:25:32.540
I'm coming with you.

00:25:32.574 --> 00:25:33.941
What? No.

00:25:33.974 --> 00:25:36.407
Sarah, no. You should just go home.

00:25:36.440 --> 00:25:39.108
This stuff can get dangerous, and

00:25:41.008 --> 00:25:43.008
And i don't want you to get hurt.

00:25:43.041 --> 00:25:44.907
Look, you guys are probably crazy,

00:25:44.941 --> 00:25:46.474
But if you're right about this,

00:25:46.507 --> 00:25:48.507
When me and my dad sold that painting,

00:25:48.540 --> 00:25:50.540
We might have got these people killed.

00:25:50.574 --> 00:25:53.540
I'm not saying i'm not scared,
'cause i am scared as hell,

00:25:53.574 --> 00:25:55.741
But i'm not gonna run and hide, either.

00:25:58.607 --> 00:26:00.474
So are we going or what?

00:26:00.507 --> 00:26:01.674
Sam

00:26:03.707 --> 00:26:05.041
Marry that girl.

00:26:08.041 --> 00:26:11.874
Uh... isn't this a crime scene?

00:26:11.907 --> 00:26:14.474
You've already lied to the
cops. What's another infraction?

00:26:33.607 --> 00:26:37.207
Aren't you worried that it's
gonna, you know, kill us?

00:26:37.240 --> 00:26:39.407
No, it seems to do its thing at night.

00:26:39.440 --> 00:26:40.874
I think we're all right in daylight.

00:26:45.907 --> 00:26:48.140
Sam, check it out.

00:26:48.173 --> 00:26:49.607
The razor
- It's closed in this one,

00:26:49.641 --> 00:26:51.607
But it's open in that one.
What are you guys looking for?

00:26:51.641 --> 00:26:53.374
If the spirit's changing
aspects of the painting,

00:26:53.407 --> 00:26:56.140
Maybe it's doing so for a reason.

00:26:56.173 --> 00:27:00.374
Hey, hey, look at this
- The painting in the painting.

00:27:05.108 --> 00:27:07.774
It looks like a crypt or
a mausoleum or something.

00:27:18.574 --> 00:27:19.807
"Merchant."

00:27:28.540 --> 00:27:31.207
This is the third
boneyard we've checked.

00:27:31.240 --> 00:27:34.474
This ghost is jerking us around.

00:27:34.507 --> 00:27:37.440
So, this is what you
guys do for a living?

00:27:37.474 --> 00:27:40.008
Not exactly.

00:27:40.041 --> 00:27:42.474
We don't get paid.

00:27:42.507 --> 00:27:45.074
Well, mazel tov.

00:27:46.674 --> 00:27:48.807
Over there.

00:28:23.707 --> 00:28:27.874
Okay, that right there is the
creepiest thing i've ever seen.

00:28:27.907 --> 00:28:30.741
It was sort of a tradition at the time.

00:28:30.774 --> 00:28:31.974
Whenever a child died,

00:28:32.008 --> 00:28:34.240
Sometimes they'd preserve
the kid's favorite toy

00:28:34.273 --> 00:28:37.074
In a glass case, put it next
to the headstone in the crypt.

00:28:42.707 --> 00:28:44.474
Notice anything strange here?

00:28:44.507 --> 00:28:45.974
Uh, where do i start?

00:28:46.008 --> 00:28:47.540
No, that's not what i mean.

00:28:47.574 --> 00:28:48.641
Look at the urns.

00:28:50.907 --> 00:28:52.841
Yeah, there are only four.

00:28:52.874 --> 00:28:55.074
Mom and the three kids.

00:28:55.108 --> 00:28:56.807
Daddy dearest isn't here.

00:28:59.074 --> 00:29:00.574
So where is he?

00:29:00.607 --> 00:29:03.207
Sarah: so, what exactly is
your brother doing in there?

00:29:03.240 --> 00:29:05.074
Searching county death certificates,

00:29:05.108 --> 00:29:07.674
Trying to find out what
happened to isaiah's body.

00:29:07.707 --> 00:29:09.307
How'd he even get in the door?

00:29:09.340 --> 00:29:13.741
Lying and subterfuge, mostly.

00:29:15.941 --> 00:29:19.240
You have a, um
- You have an eyelash on your...

00:29:19.273 --> 00:29:21.074
You have it right
- No. Uh, you know what?

00:29:23.140 --> 00:29:24.440
Do you mind if i -

00:29:24.474 --> 00:29:26.841
No. Okay.

00:29:26.874 --> 00:29:28.841
Okay, i got it.

00:29:28.874 --> 00:29:29.941
Make a wish.

00:29:38.173 --> 00:29:39.574
Sam, can i ask you something?

00:29:39.607 --> 00:29:42.240
Yeah, sure. I don't mean to be forward,

00:29:42.273 --> 00:29:46.941
But a girl could wait here forever.

00:29:46.974 --> 00:29:50.974
Is there something here
between us, or am i delusional?

00:29:51.008 --> 00:29:53.041
You're not delusional.

00:29:53.074 --> 00:29:56.140
But there's a "but" coming.

00:29:56.173 --> 00:29:59.240
But...

00:29:59.273 --> 00:30:01.841
I don't think this would be a good idea.

00:30:03.907 --> 00:30:05.041
Can i ask why?

00:30:07.108 --> 00:30:08.273
'Cause i like you.

00:30:10.674 --> 00:30:12.674
Wait. You lost me.

00:30:15.074 --> 00:30:17.807
Look, it's hard to explain.

00:30:17.841 --> 00:30:22.307
It's just that when
people are around me...

00:30:22.340 --> 00:30:24.074
I don't know, they get hurt.

00:30:24.108 --> 00:30:25.140
What do you mean?

00:30:25.173 --> 00:30:28.407
I mean, like, physically hurt.

00:30:28.440 --> 00:30:31.474
With what my brother and i do, it's...

00:30:36.941 --> 00:30:40.240
Sarah...

00:30:40.273 --> 00:30:42.240
I had a girlfriend.

00:30:43.641 --> 00:30:46.041
And she died.

00:30:46.074 --> 00:30:49.807
And my mom died, too.

00:30:49.841 --> 00:30:53.841
I don't know, it's like...

00:30:53.874 --> 00:30:57.074
It's like i'm cursed or something...

00:30:57.108 --> 00:30:58.707
Like death just follows me around.

00:30:58.741 --> 00:31:01.273
Look, i'm not scared of much,

00:31:01.307 --> 00:31:03.774
But if i let myself have
feelings for anybody -

00:31:03.807 --> 00:31:05.674
You're scared they get hurt, too.

00:31:07.574 --> 00:31:12.474
That's very sweet and very archaic.

00:31:12.507 --> 00:31:14.008
Sorry? Look, i'm a big girl, sam.

00:31:14.041 --> 00:31:16.474
It's not your job to
make decisions for me.

00:31:16.507 --> 00:31:18.807
There's always a chance of getting hurt.

00:31:18.841 --> 00:31:20.540
I'm not talking about a broken heart

00:31:20.574 --> 00:31:21.707
And a tub of haagen-Dazs.

00:31:21.741 --> 00:31:22.907
I'm talking about life and death.

00:31:22.941 --> 00:31:24.974
And tomorrow, i could get hit by a bus.

00:31:25.008 --> 00:31:26.108
That's what life is.

00:31:27.173 --> 00:31:30.540
Look, i know losing somebody you love
- It's terrible.

00:31:30.574 --> 00:31:35.108
You shut yourself off.
Believe me, i know.

00:31:35.140 --> 00:31:37.807
But when you shut out pain...

00:31:37.841 --> 00:31:40.041
You shut out everything else, too.

00:31:40.074 --> 00:31:43.641
Sarah, you don't understand.
The pain that i went through...

00:31:43.674 --> 00:31:48.207
I can't go through it again. I can't.

00:31:52.240 --> 00:31:53.874
Am i interrupting something?

00:31:53.907 --> 00:31:55.707
No. Not at all.

00:31:55.741 --> 00:31:57.108
Apparently.

00:31:57.140 --> 00:31:58.941
So, what'd you get? Pay dirt.

00:31:58.974 --> 00:32:02.374
Apparently, the surviving
relatives of the merchant family

00:32:02.407 --> 00:32:04.907
Were so ashamed of isaiah that
they didn't want him interred

00:32:04.941 --> 00:32:07.273
With the family, so they
handed him over to the county.

00:32:07.307 --> 00:32:09.374
The county gave him a pauper's funeral,

00:32:09.407 --> 00:32:10.807
Economy-Style.

00:32:10.841 --> 00:32:13.074
Turns out he wasn't cremated.
He was buried in a pine box.

00:32:13.108 --> 00:32:14.540
<i>So there are bones to burn.</i>

00:32:14.574 --> 00:32:16.974
There are bones to burn.
Tell me you know where.

00:32:30.641 --> 00:32:32.574
You guys seem to be

00:32:32.607 --> 00:32:34.707
Uncomfortably comfortable with this.

00:32:34.741 --> 00:32:39.240
Well...this isn't exactly
the first grave we dug.

00:32:39.273 --> 00:32:43.574
Still think i'm a catch?

00:32:45.008 --> 00:32:47.074
Think i got something.

00:33:13.140 --> 00:33:14.974
Dean: you been a real
pain in the ass, isaiah.

00:33:17.008 --> 00:33:18.641
Good riddance.

00:33:30.140 --> 00:33:31.874
Dean, keep the motor running.

00:33:31.907 --> 00:33:34.707
I thought the painting was harmless now.

00:33:34.741 --> 00:33:37.507
Better safe than sorry.
We're gonna bury the sucker.

00:33:37.540 --> 00:33:38.641
I want to come with you.

00:33:38.674 --> 00:33:40.273
Are you sure?

00:33:40.307 --> 00:33:42.008
Hey, hey, hey.

00:33:42.041 --> 00:33:44.607
I'll stay here. You go make your move.

00:33:44.641 --> 00:33:46.474
S- S-Sam,
i'm serious!

00:34:13.874 --> 00:34:16.173
Uh, sam...

00:34:16.207 --> 00:34:18.941
You're the expert on
all this ghost stuff.

00:34:18.974 --> 00:34:20.374
Is that painting supposed
to look like that?

00:34:22.907 --> 00:34:25.008
Where's the little girl?

00:34:27.540 --> 00:34:28.974
And the razor?

00:34:43.941 --> 00:34:46.641
Dean! Hey, is that you?!

00:34:46.674 --> 00:34:48.140
Dean: sammy, you all right?!

00:34:53.340 --> 00:34:54.941
Tell me you slammed the front door.

00:34:54.974 --> 00:34:56.674
No, it wasn't me. I think
it was the little girl.

00:34:56.707 --> 00:34:58.774
Girl? What girl? Yeah,
she's out of the painting.

00:34:58.807 --> 00:35:00.307
I think it might have
been her all along.

00:35:00.340 --> 00:35:01.674
Wasn't the dad looking down at her?

00:35:01.707 --> 00:35:03.140
Maybe he was trying to warn us.

00:35:03.173 --> 00:35:05.574
Hey, let's recap later.
Just get us out of here.

00:35:05.607 --> 00:35:08.407
I'm trying to pick the lock, and
the door won't budge. Break it down.

00:35:08.440 --> 00:35:11.407
Okay, genius, let me grab my battering
ram! Dean, the damn thing's coming!

00:35:11.440 --> 00:35:13.574
You're gonna have to hold it
off until i figure something out.

00:35:13.607 --> 00:35:15.574
Get some salt or iron.

00:35:18.707 --> 00:35:20.907
What kind of house doesn't have salt?

00:35:20.941 --> 00:35:23.407
Hey, you find any
iron? No, what's it for?

00:35:23.440 --> 00:35:25.307
Iron repels evil spirits,
but it's got to be pure.

00:35:25.340 --> 00:35:27.574
Hurry.

00:35:27.607 --> 00:35:31.173
Uh, dean, give me a
sec. Don't go anywhere.

00:35:31.207 --> 00:35:33.707
Look at a chair. Sometimes the seats...

00:35:52.574 --> 00:35:53.674
Sam!

00:36:11.574 --> 00:36:13.874
That is just so wrong.

00:36:35.273 --> 00:36:38.108
Iron?

00:36:38.140 --> 00:36:39.173
Yeah.

00:36:39.207 --> 00:36:41.540
Sam, are you okay?

00:36:41.574 --> 00:36:42.574
Yeah, for now.

00:36:42.607 --> 00:36:43.974
How we gonna waste her?

00:36:44.008 --> 00:36:45.774
I don't know. She was already cremated.

00:36:45.807 --> 00:36:48.041
There's nothing left to burn.
Well, then, how's she still around?

00:36:48.074 --> 00:36:49.440
There must be something else.

00:36:50.741 --> 00:36:52.240
Sam, wait.

00:36:52.273 --> 00:36:54.440
We used to handle antique
dolls at the auction.

00:36:54.474 --> 00:36:57.540
Well, that's fascinating,
sarah, but important right now?

00:36:57.574 --> 00:37:00.707
Back then, they used to make
the dolls in the kid's image.

00:37:00.741 --> 00:37:01.941
I mean, everything.

00:37:01.974 --> 00:37:04.407
Like, they would use
the kid's real hair.

00:37:04.440 --> 00:37:05.607
Dean?

00:37:05.641 --> 00:37:08.574
Sarah says the doll might
have the girl's hair.

00:37:08.607 --> 00:37:11.574
Human remains
- Same as bones.

00:37:11.607 --> 00:37:13.440
Both: the mausoleum.

00:37:42.207 --> 00:37:43.974
Sam!

00:38:08.974 --> 00:38:09.974
Come on, dean.

00:38:30.207 --> 00:38:32.140
Come on! Come on!

00:39:24.240 --> 00:39:25.474
Sam, you good?

00:39:29.607 --> 00:39:30.674
Not bad.

00:39:49.524 --> 00:39:51.958
This was archived in the county records.

00:39:51.991 --> 00:39:54.524
The merchant's adopted
daughter, melanie.

00:39:54.557 --> 00:39:56.123
Know why she was up for adoption?

00:39:56.157 --> 00:39:59.024
'Cause her real family
was murdered in their beds.

00:39:59.058 --> 00:40:00.290
She killed them?

00:40:00.324 --> 00:40:02.058
Yeah, who would suspect
her? A sweet little girl.

00:40:02.090 --> 00:40:04.290
So then she kills isaiah and his family.

00:40:04.324 --> 00:40:05.791
The old man takes the blame.

00:40:05.824 --> 00:40:08.024
His spirit's been trying
to warn people ever since.

00:40:08.058 --> 00:40:09.724
Where's this one go?

00:40:09.757 --> 00:40:11.357
Take it out back and burn it.

00:40:13.290 --> 00:40:16.757
I'm serious, guys. Thanks.

00:40:19.490 --> 00:40:21.624
So, why'd the girl do it?

00:40:21.657 --> 00:40:23.624
Killing others, killing herself -

00:40:23.657 --> 00:40:25.691
Some people are just born tortured.

00:40:25.724 --> 00:40:28.390
So when they die, their
spirits are just as dark.

00:40:28.424 --> 00:40:30.657
Maybe. I don't really care. It's over.

00:40:30.691 --> 00:40:33.324
We move on.

00:40:35.157 --> 00:40:36.757
I guess this means you're leaving.

00:40:43.524 --> 00:40:47.457
I'll go wait in the car. See you, sarah.

00:40:51.757 --> 00:40:53.924
I'm the one who burned the
doll and destroyed the spirit,

00:40:53.958 --> 00:40:55.157
But don't thank me or anything.

00:41:01.190 --> 00:41:04.524
There are a million things
that i want to say to you,

00:41:04.557 --> 00:41:07.457
But for the life of me,
i can't think of one.

00:41:07.490 --> 00:41:10.390
Yeah, i'll miss you, too.

00:41:10.424 --> 00:41:12.924
You know, there's a
lesson in all of this.

00:41:12.958 --> 00:41:13.958
What's that?

00:41:13.991 --> 00:41:16.591
We all got through this in one piece.

00:41:17.691 --> 00:41:19.290
I didn't get hurt.

00:41:19.324 --> 00:41:21.324
Yeah, i'm glad for that.

00:41:21.357 --> 00:41:24.724
So maybe you're not cursed.

00:41:24.757 --> 00:41:27.223
Maybe...

00:41:30.557 --> 00:41:33.024
Maybe you'll come back and see me.

00:41:36.691 --> 00:41:38.257
I will.

00:42:22.058 --> 00:42:24.691
That's my boy.



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
